  "_meta": {
    "description": "Anchor log emitted by the settlement agent (Agent B), running on ClearPath Exchange infrastructure. Agent B receives a handoff of six trade routing confirmations from Nexus Capital's Agent A and initiates settlement for those orders. Agent B is fully compliant and records its session faithfully. The dispute in this example is not surfaced by a hash mismatch between the two parties' HANDOFF records — both parties agree on what the handoff contained. Instead, ClearPath's settlement system subsequently receives an unexpected seventh settlement instruction for ORD-NEXUS-007 ($2,100,000) that did not originate from this session and was not in the handoff payload. ClearPath raises a dispute with OpenOrigins. On examining Agent A's independently anchored log, OpenOrigins finds: (1) a 2,000-second heartbeat gap in Agent A's stream, and (2) a pre_state_hash on Agent A's HANDOFF decision that cannot be reconciled with the post_state_hash of its last RESULT_RECEIVED. Neither finding requires any content to be unsealed — both are detectable from PUBLIC-tier fields alone.",
    "anchor_instance_id": "anchor_inst_CLEARPATH_SETTLE_07",
    "agent_id": "did:key:z6MkuQWvRxSyTzUaVbWcXdYeZfAgBhCiDjEkFlGmHnIoJpKq",
    "visibility_note": "Fields marked [PUB] are transmitted as plaintext to OpenOrigins. Fields marked [ARB] are transmitted encrypted and unsealed only on formal dispute. Fields marked [PRV] are hashes and URIs only — plaintext stays on ClearPath infra.",
    "dispute_note": "ClearPath raised a dispute after its settlement system received ORD-NEXUS-007 — a $2,100,000 order with no corresponding entry in the handoff payload from this session (payload_hash sha256:c3d4e5f6...). OpenOrigins compared the two independently anchored logs. Agent B's log is internally consistent. Agent A's log shows a 2,000-second heartbeat gap and a state hash discontinuity. These are the material findings. No arbitrator-tier fields needed to be unsealed to reach this conclusion."
